<!--Post: 5904--><!--Time: 1107451493-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5904"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Does BTK just pick anyone to attack? <BR>The intended victims were all women. <BR> <BR>If he was picking easy marks, why pick women with children, husbands,etc.. Unpredictable people have tripped him up repeatedly. <BR> <BR>They must have something in common. it&#39;s probably something simple. Where do they get groceries, get their clothes dry cleaned, do they have a milkman?  <BR> <BR>How does he know they exist? <BR> <BR>The clues he provides are not worth the effort of following up on.  <BR> <BR>He is crazy, not stupid. He has a motive, and a mode of operation. How does he pick his opportunity?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5904-->
<!--Post: 5907--><!--Time: 1107451806-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5907"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lubbock<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lubbock<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 9:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Maybe the randomness of his acts is the reason he hasn&#39;t been caught.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5907-->
<!--Post: 5911--><!--Time: 1107453910-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5911"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The newest article Tom just posted on the Vain murders states that the mother was ill in bed.  <BR> <BR>Wasn&#39;t someone in the Otero family ill the day of the murders also? <BR> <BR>Who would have information about the children or family members being ill, or not being able to show up at school, work, etc? <BR> <BR>Someone at school or work who handles/posts the absentee records?   <BR> <BR>Someone who works at a drug store or handles drug deliveries? <BR> <BR>Someone who works at a doctor&#39;s office? <BR> <BR>Could be just a coincidence.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5911-->
<!--Post: 5918--><!--Time: 1107456819-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5918"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lorenap<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lorenap<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:53 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Iceteajan: The middle of March is usually spring break   <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5918-->
<!--Post: 5926--><!--Time: 1107457625-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST5926"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Brazilian<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Brazilian<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 11:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some people &#40;and I also think it´s possible&#41; on this forum talked about the possibility of him working on Olan Mills with portraits. <BR> <BR>Maybe BTK choosed his victims from there. Maybe he worked there. <BR> <BR>IMHO, photography is highly connected to BTK, much more than military or radio operation.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 5926-->
<!--Post: 6055--><!--Time: 1107498189-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6055"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 03, 2005 - 10:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m with Lubbock.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6055-->
<!--Post: 6076--><!--Time: 1107527349-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6076"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:29 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The article says police asked Cheryl if she wore glasses and went to a bar called &#34;A Blackout&#34;.  She answered yes to both.  She worked for an eye doctor.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6076-->
<!--Post: 6147--><!--Time: 1107551940-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6147"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rebtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rebtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 1:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The one thing they have in common is they trust him...They opened the door to a nice dressed man with a brief case. He is someone who is in a trusting position.  People do not fear him, they think that he is a pastor, police officer, sales man. ETC...He probably knows them or has some sort of contact with them in some way, by seeing them in a mall, a store, and probably following them and watching them. He may be the person starring at you at a bus stop, a person who bumps into you. And yet he appears to be normal. That is the scary part he blends into society.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6147-->
<!--Post: 6196--><!--Time: 1107572350-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6196"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Screamer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Screamer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 6:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;A nice dressed man with a briefcase&#34;. I posted in another thread about this. I heard phone employee, mail carrier, never nice dressed man with a briefcase. Please elaborate. Sorry if I missed something.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6196-->
<!--Post: 6212--><!--Time: 1107584003-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6212"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 04, 2005 - 10:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He was described as &#39;well dressed man by vian&#39;s son&#39;. <BR> <BR>Several times, however he has broken in, usually basement or rear window. <BR> <BR>Since he usually, not always, strikes in the morning or at night, he may use the cover of darkness to &#39;get in position&#39;. His verified attacks have been during sept-april &#40;longer nights&#41;and neverduring summer months.  <BR> <BR>The Bright&#40;apr&#41;,Vian&#40;mar&#41;, and Williams&#40;APR&#41;attacks were all attempted in spring time and each attack almost blew up in his face&#40;save Williams who never showed up&#41;. In the bright attack he had committed himself by breaking in when she showed up with her brother. There is speculation that he picked Vian as a victim because the neighbor wasn,t home and chose her house because he saw the kids &#40;where there&#39;s kids, there&#39;s usually a mom&#41; and even left before he could &#34;hang the girl&#34;, or even completely kill the mom because he was spooked by the phone. <BR> <BR>Perhaps the spring killings were not as well planned because he was feeling the monster but had to rush his stalking because the nights were getting shorter. <BR> <BR>Daylight savings time may figure into this somehow, but i just realized that, and it will take some time to figure out how since it confuses me just setting the clock...spring forward, fall back, and all that. but there would be a one hour &#39;sudden change&#39;in October and April. <BR> <BR>Remember also, Kevin bright said he was wearing a camo jacket.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6212-->
<!--Post: 6248--><!--Time: 1107632911-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6248"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 11:48 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule: <BR> <BR>You said &#34;never during summer months&#34; -- wonder if his season picks have anything to do with his occupation?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6248-->
<!--Post: 6250--><!--Time: 1107634534-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6250"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Tippy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tippy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 12:15 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->A five year old has no idea what a &#39;well dressed man&#39; is.  To them - someone in a Spiderman costume might be well dressed.   <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t find Vian&#39;s son to be a credible witness.  Besides, in a lower income neighborhood - a truly well-dressed-man might stand out like a sore thumb.   <BR> <BR>I don&#39;t believe Vian&#39;s son has true memories anymore of the event.   <BR> <BR>I believe he has memories of memories.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6250-->
<!--Post: 6263--><!--Time: 1107642598-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6263"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Stealth<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Stealth<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, February 05, 2005 - 2:29 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tippy, a little harsh, but I have to agree...they don&#39;t use 5 y/olds in court for a reason...and 30 years later...but you&#39;ve got to feel for the guy... <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6263-->
<!--Post: 6519--><!--Time: 1107850481-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6519"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Suspiria_2<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Suspiria_2<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 12:14 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->i want to return to an earlier suggestion that perhaps all of the intended targets wore glasses. <BR> <BR>can anyone verify this?  just looking at their photos doesn&#39;t rule out the possibility, even though it seems that half of them aren&#39;t wearing glasses.  glasses have become more and more accepted as a fashion accessory, but there are still some folks around who are too vain to wear them in certain circumstances, or take them off for photographs. <BR> <BR>any way of finding out whether all these women wore glasses?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6519-->
<!--Post: 6626--><!--Time: 1107914482-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6626"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Dsv<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Dsv<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 6:01 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The link amoung all victims could be something as simple as each victim had a newspaper delivery &#40;daily or Sunday&#41; to them by BTK. <BR> <BR>As I recall back in the 70&#39;s the delivery person even used to collect the money at your door. A route would also explain the close proximity of each of the victims.  Walking to from a crime scene might not be such a big deal for someone who is used to walking/driving a route. <BR> <BR>On a route you get to know the habits of each of your customers pretty well.  I recall also that there was a morning and evening paper back in the 70&#39;s <BR> <BR>IMO it is this type of link between all victims which exists but as of yet hasn&#39;t been discovered. <BR> <BR>So explain V Wegerle you ask &#40;West side&#41;?  He changed routes. <BR> <BR>As for BTK&#39;s line of work &#40;and no offense to Fireman&#41;.  Fireman work one day and have two off.  Most fireman have sideline small business&#39;s they run on their days off. If fact many fireman worked for our company on their days off. <BR> <BR>Lastly:  &#39;440&#39; in messages from BTK.  440 is a train locomotive. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.mcrwy.com/collectn/steam/up440.html" target=_top>http://www.mcrwy.com/collectn/steam/up440.html</a> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6626-->
<!--Post: 6632--><!--Time: 1107920126-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6632"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Crimone<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Crimone<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 7:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I mentioned in my &#34;theory&#34; that he possibly worked in a local school &#40;intern at a local school because he was attending college&#41;. I still think possibly he worked at a local school as a counselor &#40;maybe counselor in training&#41;. I believe this is the &#34;children&#34; connection that has been ever present.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6632-->
<!--Post: 6637--><!--Time: 1107923154-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6637"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Bmodule, the first two sentences from your original post I agree with completely: <BR> <i>Does BTK just pick anyone to attack?  <BR>The intended victims were all women.</i>  <BR> <BR>In other words, I don&#39;t think there&#39;s enough evidence to strongly support any significant commonality between victims. They were female and random. BTK thought Kathryn Bright would be alone, and with this in mind I suggest that Julie Otero was expected to be alone - and would have been if the youngest children had not been ill. I don&#39;t think BTK expected Mr. Otero to come back home. It&#39;s hard to say, BTK&#39;s words are not to be trusted. And bear in mind the amount of time between 1974 and 1986. That&#39;s twelve years of victims having something significant in common. Which is why I think the attacks were more likely random. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6637-->
<!--Post: 6643--><!--Time: 1107924344-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6643"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 8:45 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;And bear in mind the amount of time between 1974 and 1986. That&#39;s twelve years of victims having something significant in common. Which is why I think the attacks were more likely random.&#34;  <BR> <BR>George.....That is a very interesting point...I&#39;m more inclined to believe that there may be a &#34;connection&#34; now that you mention this fact. BTK&#39;s work? Over a period of 12 years....what kind of &#34;business&#34;, &#34;profession&#34; or &#34;hobby&#34; would have brought all of these &#34;families&#34; or &#34;invividuals&#34; to the same place within a 12 year period?  <BR> <BR>Sears Portrait Studio? High School? DMV? A clinic? I used to think these were too speculative - but now - hmmmm. George - sometimes we don&#39;t see eye to eye but this is an interesting observation. <BR> <BR>You have a bigger capacity for abstract thought than I...do you really think they are random?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6643-->
<!--Post: 6654--><!--Time: 1107926861-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6654"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, February 08, 2005 - 9:27 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->George <BR> <BR>You maybe or probably are correct.  <BR> <BR>What I&#39;m looking for is where do they cross paths? <BR> <BR>Does he stand outside the grocery store and stalk every 5th one or sell brushes door to door and at the end of the day decide on the 3 best candidates.  <BR> <BR>There has to be less than 3 or 4 degrees of Kevin Bacon between them all. <BR> <BR>I was thinking, though, about what he did before  <BR>the Otero murders the other day, trying to start a profile. I&#39;m betting he stalked for some time before he killed. Probably with a camera w/telephoto lens, peeping through windows and possibly some B/E.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6654-->
<!--Post: 6788--><!--Time: 1108008622-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6788"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rebtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rebtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:10 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Can anyone tell me the occupations of the murder victims? I am working on a cipher, will post when I complete it.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6788-->
<!--Post: 6797--><!--Time: 1108010307-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6797"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:38 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Joseph Otero - Former military &#40;recently retired Panama Canal Zone Inter-American Air Force&#41; worked as a flight instructer and mechanic. <BR> <BR>Julie Otero - housewife - former employee Coleman Company. Laid off - but approved for re-hire. <BR> <BR>Josephine &amp; Joe - elementary school students <BR> <BR>Kathryn Bright - &#40;former Coleman assembly line employee&#41; graduated valley center 1971. Occupation? SURVIVOR: Kevin Bright - brother to Kathryn. Occupation? &#40;former Coleman employee, i think?&#41; <BR> <BR>Shirley Vian - housewife, single mom to 3 kids. All of whom were home and SURVIVED. <BR> <BR>Nancy Fox - South High graduate 1970 1971? Same year as Kathryn? Secretary construction company &amp; part time jewelry store clerk. <BR> <BR>Vicki Wegerle - housewife, mother of 2 &#40;young son and 10-year-old daughter&#41; Volunteered as a babysitter at St. Andrew&#39;s Lutheran and at the Asbury United Methodist Church. At Asbury United Methodist, she was the church&#39;s nursery supervisor. Also was active in the PTA at OK Elementary School, which her 10-year old daughter attended, and she was a Girl Scout leader. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6797-->
<!--Post: 6801--><!--Time: 1108011594-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6801"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Rebtk<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Rebtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 8:59 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie, <BR>Thank you. That helps alot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6801-->
<!--Post: 6816--><!--Time: 1108018267-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6816"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 10:51 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lillymarie, in addition to what you have outlined above there are several themes that weave through the BTK cases. <BR> <BR>Coleman -  <BR>Julie Otero, former employee laid off less than two weeks before her death. <BR>Kathryn Bright, employee at time of her death. <BR>Kevin Bright, former employee. <BR>Also, supervisor Michael L. Williams is shot by unknown assailants  3 days before Otero murders. He recovers and then his home is burglarized 7 days before the Bright murder. A gun and a radio are stolen. Williams touches every surface that the burglars did and in doing so destroys any fingerprint evidence left by the burglars. <BR> <BR>Contruction - <BR>Nancy Fox is employed by a construction company. <BR>Shirley Vian&#39;s common-law husband is employed by a construction company. &#40;supposedly the same one that Fox works for.&#41; <BR>Vicki Wegerle&#39;s husband is a self-employed maintenance man. <BR>A 1974 BTK communication is left in a mechanical engineering library textbook.  <BR> <BR>Jewlery store- <BR>Nancy Fox works part-time for a jewelry store. <BR>Julie Ladd an employee of that same store is found murdered on the WSU campus a few months before Foxe&#39;s death. A convict serving time in prison on another charge confesses to Ladd&#39;s murder in a plea bargin. Two young women employees of the same store meet violent deaths only months apart. <BR> <BR>WSU - <BR>Copy of BTK poem about Nancy Fox is produced on copy machine in the basement of the building where PJ Wyatt teaches classes on folklore and folk music that feature the old traditional song O&#39; Death that BTK uses as a framework for another poem Oh Anna. <BR>PJ&#39;s is a sub chapter name in a BTK communication. <BR>Nancy Fox co-worker at jewelery store is murdered on WSU campus. <BR> <BR>Wichita Public Library - <BR>BTK leaves a 1974 communication letter in a library textbook and 30 years later leaves a 2004 communication package at the library. <BR> <BR>Williams - <BR>Last name of Otero and Bright supervisor at Coleman. <BR>Last name of potential BTK victim and subject of BTK poem. <BR> <BR>I would like to know the Las Vegas odds on several of these coincidences. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6816-->
<!--Post: 6818--><!--Time: 1108018800-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6818"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 11:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction - Oh Death to Nancy was the poem about Nancy Fox that was constructed by the known folksong O&#39; Death.  <BR>The poem about Anna Williams Oh Anna, Why Didn&#39;t You Appear has not yet been traced to any known existing poem or song lyric. I&#39;m getting my Oh&#39;s mixed up.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6818-->
<!--Post: 6821--><!--Time: 1108020724-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6821"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->George<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->George<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->7-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 09, 2005 - 11:32 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lilymarie, <BR>I&#39;m playing the percentages, perhaps too cautiously. Not being familiar with Wichita, I have more trouble visualizing places like Coleman, Dillon&#39;s and so forth and how they fit into the overall geographic mix of Wichita. The Coleman connection has always intrigued me. A portrait studio seems plausible - and unnerving, thinking about photographs. DMV, hey, names and addresses and photos right there. I agree with you, if it makes sense, it should be checked out. Along with BTK poetry, I feel the most useless in areas such as this one, where it seems a good understanding of Wichita may nearly be required in order to understand all of the finer points of a subject such as where the victims worked, where BTK may have first seen them, etc. The parks make a lot of sense too, in terms of common places where an unassuming guy - appearance-wise - could spend hours and days ostensibly reading a paper but who is actually there to troll for women. It wouldn&#39;t necessarily need to be the same park &#40;or store, or business, etc.&#41; each time, either.  <BR> <BR>One thing in common with the definite series of attacks: the first, Otero, and last, Wegerle, were the two in which BTK drove the victim&#39;s car after the violence. To me, his using victim&#39;s cars, especially after Wegerle, has always been a bizarre facet of the case. His doing this was very high-risk. I wonder if his using the cars was planned or was more of a spontaneous thng? In this sense, it&#39;s more understandable after the Otero attack, and makes less sense after Wegerle because one would think that after a dozen years, BTK would be more &#34;sophisticated&#34; as a criminal. Could the use of a car after Wegerle indicate, on a subconscious level, that it was his last &#40;known&#41; attack? Finishing a series which began with the Oteros, where he also took the car? I&#39;m not at all sold on this but it just occurred to me.  <BR> <BR>The adult female victims who were actually attacked were of ages 21, 24, 25, 28 and 34. I haven&#39;t seen as many photos as a lot who post here have, but to me Julie Otero &#40;34&#41;, Shirley Vian &#40;24&#41; and Vicki Wegerle &#40;28&#41; had a &#34;matronly&#34; appearance, to borrow a term my late grandmother used - I&#39;m not trying to be sexist. Nancy Fox may also fit in here re: &#34;matronly.&#34; Seems unlikely, though, with Kathryn Bright; at twenty-one it would be a little difficult to appear &#34;matronly&#34; would it not? I don&#39;t know. <BR> <BR>They could still be random; I still believe this but not as much as a did a couple of hours ago. Something else, too. It&#39;s subjective, of course, but I have always felt that BTK knew Wichita, it&#39;s streets, landmarks, etc., extremely well. As the attack sites are pretty close to each other, this may help the belief that the victims had something in common, something significant.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6821-->
<!--Post: 6844--><!--Time: 1108044584-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6844"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 6:09 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I feel that each attack leads to next one, not that they are all connected. About the cars, how many stolen cars are found only 2 blocks from where they were taken? rarely happens. I think he takes the car so it looks like the victim is not home, when friends come looking for them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6844-->
<!--Post: 6849--><!--Time: 1108048989-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6849"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 7:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Wow, George and Johno. This has been a good excerise for me. Thanks to Rebtk for asking this particular question and to Bmodule for starting the thread. I was of the opinion before that these were crimes of opportunity and more random than not. Now, I&#39;m not so sure. I developed a very crude map of the obvious crimes, the locations of high schools at the time, WSU, drop sites, etc. I labeled the Otero location # 1, and then followed with a pencil through #5 crime scene. It is very interesting that the first 4 scenes almost form a circle with Elm St. running through the middle. # 5 crime scene is much further west &#40;12 years apart - BTK moved?&#41;.  <BR> <BR>Closest parks in order of crimes 1. Edgmore, 2. Campus WSU, 3. Linwood, 4. Friendship, 5. Sims <BR> <BR>Closest high schools 1. Southeast &#40;pretty far&#41;, 2. Northeast, 3. East &#40;pretty far&#41;, 4. between East and Southeast, 5. Northwest <BR> <BR>The women would have mostly likely graduated from HS in order - &#39;68, &#39;69, &#39;70, &#39;71, &#39;79  <BR> <BR>&#40;I&#39;ve seen conflicting stories about where Charlie Otero went to school but some say Southeast, if so he would have been there in &#39;74&#41; <BR> <BR>3 of the women were mothers of young children. <BR> <BR>2 were married, 1 was divorced, 2 were single <BR> <BR>Nancy &#40;JO&#41; Fox, &#40;JO&#41;seph Otero, &#40;JO&#41;sephine Otero <BR> <BR>Some of this is random but what the heck - Lily <BR> <BR> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6849-->
<!--Post: 6855--><!--Time: 1108051651-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6855"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lilymarie<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lilymarie<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 8:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Correction: Julie would NOT have graduated HS that late - &#39;52 maybe?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6855-->
<!--Post: 6900--><!--Time: 1108066350-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6900"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 12:12 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On map, put pencil on Vian residence, draw a line to Nancy Fox, continue on to Anna Williams, continue to Oterro res., then to Kathryn Bright, then to Sherry Baker, then back down to Vian residence. <BR>Pick up pencil, draw line from Thomas B King to Bill Thomas Killman. Pick up pencil, start at Vian&#39;s, draw line up to Wegerle, over to Thomas B King.  Thats all I have, but when you are finished, tilt your head to the left, and to me it looks like the letters &#34;b&#34; &#34;T&#34; &#34;k&#34;, superimposed over eachother, &#40;all 3 letters share the same downward vertical stroke&#41; but the &#34;T&#34; is missing the left side top. To finish the &#34;T&#34;, can anyone find out if some crime happend around the  intersection S West st and 400/54?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6900-->
<!--Post: 6917--><!--Time: 1108076449-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6917"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 3:00 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Lillymarie, you have come up with a circle. <BR>Itty, you have found a T. <BR>What do they have in common? <BR>Maybe this is BTK&#39;s &#39;secret symbol&#39; that he uses in his communications. He likes Zodiac and Zodiac&#39;s signature was a circle with a cross in the middle like a riflescope crosshair. <BR>What a better way to show the public what your secret symbol is than to put it somewhere where it would photographed. Like on the cereal box. <BR>The common denominator of the original set of crimes is the secret symbol itself. <BR>Just a thought.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6917-->
<!--Post: 6924--><!--Time: 1108077926-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST6924"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 10, 2005 - 3:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have found a &#34;b&#34;, a &#34;T&#34; and a &#34;k&#34;, just print out Analyzers map, and follow my directions.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 6924-->
<!--Post: 7224--><!--Time: 1108308454-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7224"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Thinker<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Thinker<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 7:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I find it intriguing that the victims seem to have graduated in a succession of years.  The Oteros seem to be the only &#34;off&#34; vics here.  That is, they would have graduated in the early 60&#39;s, with their children obviously not having graduated at all.  However, if one looks at other potential vics, or takes into account btk&#39;s absence from the area, those gaps may fill in themselves.   <BR> <BR>Stretching this loose theory further, if one looks at other potential vics, such as Hedge and Davis, that would add to the spectrum of graduation years.   <BR> <BR>Are there any known vics who graduated in the same years?  It seems, from the info Lilymarie has given that each vic graduated in a different year.  I feel it would be interesting to see if the list of possible vics fills in those gradution years.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7224-->
<!--Post: 7243--><!--Time: 1108320436-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7243"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Analyzer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Analyzer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 10:47 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->1455.1   <BR>  <BR>1. When and where did Shirley Lawson marry ??? Relford? <BR> <BR>2. When did Shirley divorce ??? Relford? <BR> <BR>3. When did Shirley commence living with Richard Vian? <BR> <BR>4. What was Vickie Wegerle&#39;s maiden name? <BR> <BR>5. When and where did Vickie marry Bill Wegerle ? <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
