<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7261"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 3:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While thinking today, I pondered Occam&#39;s Razor.  <BR> <BR><a href="http://pespmc1.vub.ac.be/OCCAMRAZ.html" target=_top>http://pespmc1.vub.ac.be/OCCAMRAZ.html</a> <BR> <BR>In doing so, I came up with the one fact that we know.  BTK does BTK...in essence, abuse.  Now, the next fact is that most, if not all, abusers were abused as children. <BR> <BR>This then led me to the thought that perhaps he was being abused and his mother was aware, but did nothing...acknowledge it, prevent it, stop it, or otherwise.   <BR> <BR>Thus, this led me to think about the victims.  All of them mothers....perhaps mothers of children the ages of when BTK was being abused.  Therefore I arrived at the prospect of the commonality of the victims and the motive...punishment/retribution. <BR> <BR>Also, I thought that perhaps he had children &#40;girls&#41; of his own during the &#34;dormant stage.&#34;  It was then that he was able to abuse to enough satisfaction.   <BR> <BR>As mentioned in the previous profile, wife died or divorced him and/or children would have nothing to do with him...thus, he returned back to his former identity or Eros/Thanatos Id &#40;see Freud&#41;.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7261-->
