<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7282"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Whoisbtk<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Whoisbtk<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 8:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m still checking on Bright, but otherwise: <BR> <BR>All victims homes were built from 1920 to 1948. <BR> <BR>All homes were small.  Ground floor: Otero &#40;1947&#41; 813 sq/ft with 3 bedrooms; Fox &#40;1948&#41; 528 sq/ft, 1 bedroom; Vian 840 sq/ft, 2 bed, 2 bath; Wegerly &#40;1920&#41;, 724 sq/ft. <BR> <BR>All homes had gas heat. <BR> <BR>No homes had attached garages. <BR> <BR><a href="mailto:whoisbtk@yahoo.com">whoisbtk@yahoo.com</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
